The FujiNet Atari 7800 cartridge boots .a78 images: CONFIG mounts one and
the ESP32 (here, the RS232 PC runtime) must push it to the cartridge over the
DBC stream like any other cartridge ROM. discover_mediatype() only knows ROM,
BIN, INT and ITV (and CHF upstream), so an .a78 file mounted as a plain disk
image and the cartridge waited forever for BOOT_READY. Add A78; the
cartridge strips the header itself. Upstream as fujinet-firmware a4d40118d on
fujiversal-atari7800-board; carried here until the pin
(cmake/Dependencies.cmake) moves to a commit that has it.

--- a/lib/media/rs232/diskType.cpp
+++ b/lib/media/rs232/diskType.cpp
@@ -77,8 +77,11 @@
         // replaces the previous disksize==8192||16384||32768 heuristic
         // (rs232Disk::mount()), which misfired on any file of those exact
         // sizes regardless of extension and missed every other ROM size.
+        // A78 is an Atari 7800 image with its header, which the FujiNet
+        // 7800 cartridge strips.
         if (strcasecmp(ext, "ROM") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "BIN") == 0 ||
-            strcasecmp(ext, "INT") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "ITV") == 0)
+            strcasecmp(ext, "INT") == 0 || strcasecmp(ext, "ITV") == 0 ||
+            strcasecmp(ext, "A78") == 0)
         {
             return MEDIATYPE_ROM;
         }
